.TH CORSAIRVIRTUOSOCTL 1 2026-10-01 "linux-corsair-headset-controller" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
corsairvirtuosoctl \- control a Corsair Virtuoso RGB Wireless XT headset
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B corsairvirtuosoctl
.B status
.br
.B corsairvirtuosoctl sidetone
.BR on | off | toggle
.br
.B corsairvirtuosoctl sidetone\-volume
.I percent
.br
.B corsairvirtuosoctl brightness
.I percent
.br
.B corsairvirtuosoctl sleep\-timer
.I minutes
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B corsairvirtuosoctl
reads and changes settings on a Corsair Virtuoso RGB Wireless XT headset through its
SlipStream wireless dongle (USB ID 1b1c:0a64). It talks to the dongle directly through
the dongle's
.I /dev/hidrawN
node for USB interface 3, opening it for a single command and closing it again.
No daemon is needed.
.PP
The headset rejects writes in its default hardware mode. For each change,
.B corsairvirtuosoctl
switches the headset to software mode, writes the setting, and switches back. The
headset keeps the new value after switching back.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Show firmware version, battery level, charging state, battery voltage, whether the
USB cable is connected, mic mute state, and the current sidetone, brightness and
sleep-timer settings.
.TP
.BR sidetone " " on | off | toggle
Turn sidetone (hearing your own mic in the headset) on or off, or flip its current
state. Prints the resulting state.
.TP
.BI sidetone\-volume " percent"
Set the sidetone level, 0\(en100.
.TP
.BI brightness " percent"
Set the LED brightness, 0\(en100.
.TP
.BI sleep\-timer " minutes"
Put the headset to sleep after
.I minutes
of inactivity, 1\(en60.
.B 0
turns the timer off.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit. Each command also accepts
.BR \-h .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on success, non-zero on failure. Failures include the dongle not being found, missing
permission to open its hidraw node, no response from the headset (for example when it
is switched off), or the headset rejecting a command.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/udev/rules.d/70\-corsair\-headset.rules
udev rule that lets the logged-in user open the dongle's hidraw nodes without root.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
corsairvirtuosoctl status
corsairvirtuosoctl sidetone toggle
corsairvirtuosoctl sidetone\-volume 40
corsairvirtuosoctl sleep\-timer 15
.EE
.SH NOTES
Only the Virtuoso RGB Wireless XT is supported. The volume wheel and Bluetooth state
are handled by the headset itself and cannot be read or changed.
